Hermes Security plugin: give the plugin's skills real descriptions in the system prompt's skill index.

Attribution: hermes-security is by NousResearch (https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins, subdir hermes-security, catalog
revision 85e835c3deb972ca49cb58f7d3517b10b6672a1a, installed 0.1.3), licensed Apache-2.0. This patch is a modification of its file
hermes_security/plugin.py made by Odysseus (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)); the upstream LICENSE and NOTICE stay with the plugin.

Why: ctx.register_skill(name, path) without description/frontmatter registers an EMPTY description, so the seven hermes-security:* skills appear in
<available_skills> with nothing to select on (the REA plugin passes both). The patch reads each SKILL.md's own frontmatter with Hermes' parser and
tells the tool-backed hermes-security:security-audit apart from the guidance-only security-audit skill.

Applied by the managed component, never in place: scripts/hermes-webapp-component.py security-plugin [--apply] (staging copy, git apply --check,
compile check, original kept in the component backups folder, takes effect at the next gateway start). Plugin updates replace the file: re-apply
or upstream the change.

diff --git a/hermes_security/plugin.py b/hermes_security/plugin.py
--- a/hermes_security/plugin.py
+++ b/hermes_security/plugin.py
@@ -8,6 +8,21 @@
 _SERVICE_LOCK = Lock()
 _SKILLS = ("security-audit", "security-diff-review", "threat-model", "validate-finding",
            "fix-finding", "verify-fix", "define-security-policy")
+
+
+# The generic `security-audit` skill (guidance only) shares this name; say which one drives the tool-backed scan.
+_HINTS = {"security-audit": " Tool-backed: runs the security_scan_* scan with evidence and coverage tracking (the plain security-audit skill is guidance only)."}
+
+
+def _skill_metadata(path, name):
+    """Description and frontmatter for the system prompt's skill index (register_skill does not read them from SKILL.md by itself)."""
+    try:
+        from agent.skill_utils import parse_frontmatter
+        data, _ = parse_frontmatter(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
+        description = str(data.get("description") or "").strip()
+        return (description + _HINTS.get(name, "")).strip(), dict(data)
+    except Exception:
+        return "", {}
 
 
 def get_service(ctx=None):
@@ -48,4 +63,5 @@
             ctx.register_hook(name, callback)
     skill_root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "skills"
     for name in _SKILLS:
-        ctx.register_skill(name, skill_root / name / "SKILL.md")
+        description, frontmatter = _skill_metadata(skill_root / name / "SKILL.md", name)
+        ctx.register_skill(name, skill_root / name / "SKILL.md", description=description, frontmatter=frontmatter)
